  "changelog": "Deep Research Forge 0.1.0 \u2013 Initial Release\n\n- Introduces a structured, evidence-led skill for deep research, analysis, and decision briefs on products, companies, concepts, technologies, or cultural phenomena.\n- Supports method-driven workflows: define research questions, build an evidence ledger, map citations, analyze timelines, compare competitors, and assess mechanisms.\n- Enables optional multi-agent parallel research with clear roles (integrator, source scout, timeline analyst, dissent reviewer, etc.), independent evidence tracking, and conflict resolution.\n- Distinguishes output by user intent, from concise research orientation to full deep-dive reports, decision briefs, asset packs, and research retrospectives.\n- Emphasizes traceable sources, claim-level citation, separation of fact/inference/judgment, research quality scoring, and actionable next steps.",
